# Playmaker — Authors

This file records individuals who have contributed original work to the Playmaker project.

## Authors

| Name                | GitHub                | Since      | Team Name              |
| ------------------- | --------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------- |
| Pranav Dharanipathy | `@PranavDharanipathy` | 2026-09-17 | Athletech Robotics     |

### Fields

* **Name** — The author's name.
* **GitHub** — The author's GitHub username.
* **Since** — The date on which the author first contributed original work to the Playmaker project.
* **Team** — The team, organization, or group the author was affiliated with when making their contribution.

The **Authors** section is a record of project contributors and does not, by itself, grant any additional copyright or licensing rights beyond those otherwise applicable to the author's contributions.

## Original Author

**Pranav Dharanipathy**

Pranav Dharanipathy is recognized as the **Original Author** of Playmaker for purposes of `ADDITIONAL-PERMISSIONS`.

The Original Author's additional permissions are perpetual and irrevocable and are not affected by changes to this file.

## Esteemed Authors

The following individuals are currently designated as **Esteemed Authors**:

| Name | GitHub | Designated |
| ---- | ------ | ---------- |
| —    | —      | —          |

An individual is an **Esteemed Author** only while they are listed in this section.

Esteemed Author status grants the individual the additional permissions described in `ADDITIONAL-PERMISSIONS`.

## Designation

An individual may be designated as an Esteemed Author through an authorized decision of the CleatsPL organization.

The designation becomes effective when the individual's name is added to the **Esteemed Authors** section of this file through an authorized project change.

## Revocation

An Esteemed Author designation may be revoked through an authorized decision of the CleatsPL organization.

The designation is revoked when the individual's name is removed from the **Esteemed Authors** section through an authorized project change.

Upon revocation, the additional permissions associated with Esteemed Author status cease in accordance with `ADDITIONAL-PERMISSIONS`.

Revocation does not retroactively invalidate any lawful actions, distributions, copies, or derivative works made while the individual held Esteemed Author status.

